                <pb facs="0557" n="459" sameAs="frus:frus1920v01/pg459"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">893.002/55: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Minister in China</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Crane</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to
                        the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Peking</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1920-08-12T12:00:00+08:00"><hi rendition="#italic">August 12,
                                1920—noon</hi></date>.<lb/>[Received August 12—3:50
                    a.m.]</dateline></opener>
                <p>218. My 217. Following Cabinet announced by President’s proclamation 11th:</p>
                <p>Minister of War, Chin Yun Peng; Navy, Sa Chen Ping; Foreign Affairs, Yen Hui
                    Ching; Interior, Chang Chih Tan; Education, Fan Yuan Lien; Justice, Tung Keng;
                    Finance, Chow Tze Chi; Communications, Yeh Kung Cho, Agriculture and Commerce,
                    Wang Nai Pin.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Crane</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
